    "solution": [
      [
        "1/6",
        "Let's make the fractions equivalent first. The least common denominator of 3 and 12 is 12."
      ],
      [
        "2/6",
        "Write $5\\frac{2}{3}$ with 12 as the denominator by multiplying the numerator and denominator by 4. $5\\frac{2}{3} = 5\\frac{8}{12}$"
      ],
      [
        "3/6",
        "Now add. Remember to add whole numbers to whole numbers and fractions to fractions."
      ],
      [
        "4/6",
        "$5\\frac{8}{12}+3\\frac{1}{12}=8\\frac{9}{12}$"
      ],
      [
        "5/6",
        "Now simplify. $8\\frac{9}{12}=8\\frac{3}{4}$"
      ],
      [
        "6/6",
        "Write the answer. $5\\frac{2}{3}+3\\frac{1}{12}=8\\frac{3}{4}$"
      ]
